1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,490
Slide 15 exposes THE BATTERY DRAIN PARADOX. James, why did your laptop die on that cross-country flight?

2
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,331
True story, students!

3
00:00:10,331 --> 00:00:16,922
I was flying from New York to San Francisco with a full battery that should have lasted 8 hours.

4
00:00:16,922 --> 00:00:21,180
Four hours into the flight, my laptop battery hit 5% and died!

5
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,530
And what was draining the power, James?

6
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:32,337
Look at Card 1 on screen: Chromium's JavaScript event loop uses high-precision timers ticking every 15 milliseconds!

7
00:00:32,337 --> 00:00:37,190
That prevented my Intel CPU from ever entering deep C-State low-power sleep!

8
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:49,690
And look at Card 2: the floating search bar's transparent drop-shadow required constant DirectX GPU composition, keeping the GPU drawing 35 watts of power even with the screen closed!

9
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:56,550
Look at Card 3: a 40% battery penalty just to keep an idle search bar waiting in the background!

10
00:00:56,950 --> 00:01:03,650
Efficiency is not just a software metric; it is the physical stewardship of battery life and energy.

